title: "RL-CAT: a 12-DOF quadruped robot with an open, end-to-end RL pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A complete open-source 12-DOF quadruped platform: mechanical design, electronics,
  STM32 real-time firmware (100 Hz), Raspberry Pi 5 policy runtime, ESP32-C3 wireless
  bridge, and a legged_gym-based reinforcement learning pipeline.
  This release documents a quantified "stand on the ground" milestone
  (reach error 1.23 deg, drift 0.00 deg) together with a detailed catalogue of the
  25 engineering pitfalls encountered on the way to it.
  Sim-to-real locomotion is work in progress.
type: software
